re](https://www.elephanthaferry.in/)).  \n\n**Nightlife:**  \n- **Bandra Bandstand** (Live music at *The Bombay Club*; try *Whiskey & Soda* at *The Bar at The Park Hyatt*).  \n\n---\n\n### **Day 3: Fort Mumbai & Coastal Vibe**  \n**Morning:**  \n- **Fort Mumbai** (Visit the 17th-century *Bandra Fort* and *St. Andrew’s Church*; lesser-known colonial sites).  \n- **City of Dreams Museum** (Interactive history of Mumbai; [book tickets](https://www.cityofdreamsmuseum.com)).  \n\n**Afternoon:**  \n- **Lunch at Indian Restaurant (Fort)** (1880s eatery; try *Prawn Cutlet* and *Bread Omlette*).  \n- **Jewish Quarter Walk** (Chhatrapati Sambhaji Nagar; visit the *Chabad House Synagogue* and *Bombay Jewish Museum*).  \n\n**Evening:**  \n- **Juhu Beach** (Watch sunset; grab *Pani Puri* from local vendors).  \n- **Final Dinner at Shakti (Juhu)** (Modern Indian cuisine; book the *Rooftop Terrace* for ocean views).  \n\n**Nightlife:**  \n- **Club Cub (Bandra)** (Iconic Mumbai club; check [event calendar](https://www.clubcub.in) for DJ sets).  \n\n---\n\n### **Mid-Range Stays**  \n- **Taj Heritage Select Hotel, Mumbai** ([Website](https://www.tajhotels.com); Colonial-era building, central location).  \n- **Oberoi Mumbai** ([Website](https://www.oberoihotels.com); Luxury with heritage charm, 5-minute walk to CST).  \n\n---\n\n### **Local Tips**  \n1. **January Weather:** 18–25°C; pack light layers for evening breezes.  \n2. **Transport:** Use Uber/Metro for convenience; avoid local trains during peak hours.  \n3. **Reservations:** Book ferry tickets for Elephanta Caves 2 weeks in advance.  \n4. **Safety:** Avoid isolated areas at night; stick to well-lit zones like Colaba/Bandra.  \n5. **Food Alerts:** Check [Zomato](https://www.zomato.com/mumbai) for real-time restaurant ratings.  \n\n*For last-minute updates on events or closures, recheck 1 week before departure.* 🏛️🌃'}}
